      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Why 2 minutes, when we could have infinite minutes?\nIt used to be there was a good reason for limiting the length of emotes.  That being there was no way to cancel out of them. \nNow that we can cancel out of them by moving however, there seems to no longer be any reason to have a limit on length. And having a limit on length just means that if we need to exceed 60 seconds in an animation, we have to create a duplicate of our avatar and play the animation on that, which thanks to the performance ranking system, is no longer a good idea.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
